/-!
# The formal glueing situation at the étale local rings

Let `D` be the formal glueing situation of Stacks 0AEV: `f : Y ⟶ X` quasi-compact and
quasi-separated, `Z ⊆ X` a closed subspace of finite presentation, `f` an isomorphism over `Z`
and flat at the points of `f⁻¹(Z)`. Let `ȳ` be a geometric point of `Y` lying on `f⁻¹(Z)`, with
image `x̄ = f ∘ ȳ`, and write `R = 𝒪_{X, x̄}` and `S' = 𝒪_{Y, ȳ}`, an `R`-algebra through the
canonical homomorphism of étale local rings. On an affine pointed étale chart of `X` at `x̄` let
`g₁, …, g_r` be regular functions whose common zero locus is the part of the chart lying over
`Z`, and let `J ⊆ R` be the ideal generated by their germs.

This file proves that `R → S'` is flat and that `R / J → S' / JS'` is an isomorphism: these are
the two hypotheses of Stacks 05ER at the stalks, which is how the source checks Stacks 0AF0 "by
looking at stalks". It also proves that such a chart and such functions exist at every geometric
point of `X`.

## Main results

* `FormalGlueing.bijective_quotientMap_of_pow_le`: for a flat `R → S`, bijectivity of
  `R / I → S / IS` passes to every ideal `J` containing a power of `I`.
* `FormalGlueing.exists_mul_eq_zero_isUnit_algebraMap`: an element of `A` dying in a flat local
  `A`-algebra is killed by an element whose image is a unit.
* `FormalGlueing.bijective_quotientMap_ker_of_tensor_flat`: the algebra of a cartesian square of
  local rings whose tensor comparison is flat and whose closed part is an isomorphism.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.bijective_etaleLocalRingMap_of_isIso`: an isomorphism induces
  bijections of étale local rings.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ker_etaleLocalRingMap_le_closedSubspaceStalkIdeal`: the kernel of the
  surjection `𝒪_{X, x̄} → 𝒪_{Z, z̄}` lies in the stalk of the defining ideal of `Z`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalGlueingSituation.flat_etaleLocalRingMap_of_mem_preimage`:
  `R → S'` is flat.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalGlueingSituation.bijective_quotientMap_etaleLocalRingMap`:
  `R / J → S' / JS'` is bijective.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalGlueingSituation.exists_chart_zeroLocus_eq`: an affine pointed
  chart and functions `g₁, …, g_r` as above exist at every geometric point of `X`.

## Implementation notes

Write `K₀` for the kernel of `R → 𝒪_{Z, z̄}`. The square with corners `f⁻¹(Z)`, `Z`, `Y`, `X` is
cartesian, so `𝒪_{f⁻¹(Z), z̄'}` is flat over `S' ⊗_R 𝒪_{Z, z̄}`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.cartesian_etaleStalk_tensor_flat`); since `f` is an isomorphism over
`Z`, `𝒪_{Z, z̄} → 𝒪_{f⁻¹(Z), z̄'}` is bijective. A flat surjection onto a local ring through
which a local homomorphism factors is injective (equational criterion of flatness), and this
gives `R / K₀ ≅ S' / K₀S'`. The kernel `K₀` lies in the stalk `I_x̄` of the ideal sheaf of `Z`,
which is generated by the germs of the defining ideal on the chart; that ideal is finitely
generated and has the same zero locus as the `gᵢ`, so a power of `I_x̄`, hence of `K₀`, lies in
`J`. Flatness then carries the isomorphism from `K₀` to `J` (Stacks 05E9 in the form
`IPowerTorsion.baseChange_bijective_iff_quotientMap_bijective`).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AEV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AEV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AF0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AF0)
